>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (Power Supply Box)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E ( I designed the internal layout and built all the wire harnesses: 9 power supplies at roughly 15 kW total, 9 power harnesses, and a CAN bus to each actuator and motor. I laid it out to fit the supplies as compactly as possible while still leaving full access to every terminal for wiring and service. It has never failed. No shorts, no wiring issues, and no downtime across more than 13,000 official 3-minute throttle blip cycles, and it still runs fine.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (Temperature Control \(PID AC\))
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E ( I put the chamber's air conditioning under closed-loop PID control by hacking its IR receiver. I harvested the AC's IR command signals and retransmitted them from an Arduino and an IR transmitter, so the controller could drive the unit directly, allowing for complete automated cycling. I tuned the loop myself and built in hysteresis so the AC compressor cycles gently instead of short-cycling, which protects its lifespan while still holding a stable test temperature.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
